\name{cellucid_analysis_pages_set}
\alias{cellucid_analysis_pages_set}
\title{Choose the pages of an analysis}
\usage{
cellucid_analysis_pages_set(viewer, analysis, pages, in_ = "panel")
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{analysis}{The analysis: markers (marker genes), differential (differential expression), dotplot, signature (gene signature), composition, quick, detailed, correlation. One of \code{"markers"}, \code{"differential"}, \code{"dotplot"}, \code{"signature"}, \code{"composition"}, \code{"quick"}, \code{"detailed"}, \code{"correlation"}. Required.}
\item{pages}{A vector or list of text (at least 1 character) (each once). Required.}
\item{in_}{Either exactly \code{"panel"} (The Analysis panel); or a whole number (at least 1) (A floating analysis window, by its number (1 is the first open)). Default \code{"panel"}, the viewer's own. Sent as the parameter \code{in}.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
The highlight pages an analysis compares (by name, "Rest of <page>" for the rest of a page's cells); nothing runs.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{analysis.pages.set} (Analysis). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{analysis}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_analysis_pages_set(viewer, analysis = "markers",
      pages = list())
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
